speechtext:
It is my duty, pursuant to provisional standing order 39A, to inform the house that the following questions to be raised at ten o'clock this day are as follows: the hon. member for Lambton West (Mr. Foy), whether agreement has been made with the United States to build a weir or dam on the St. Clair river at Sarnia to control the level of the waters in lake Huron; the hon. member for Parry Sound-Muskoka (Mr. Aiken), experiments being conducted by the United States corps of engineers directed toward cutting down the outflow of water from lake Huron at Sarnia;

Mr. Belanger (Charlevoix), the construction of harbour facilities at Riviere du Loup.

The house will now resume the business interrupted at five o'clock.
